<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Man Singh Tomar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1516</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Man Singh Tomar was the Tomara ruler of Gwalior from 1486 to 1516 and the most celebrated of his line. He resisted repeated attacks by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lodi-dynasty">Lodi</a> sultans of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> and built the Man Mandir palace in Gwalior fort, known for its blue tile work. His court was a centre of music where the dhrupad style developed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/man-singh-tomar.jpg" alt="Man Singh Tomar" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gyanendra_Singh_Chauhan · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Maharaja_Mansingh_Tomar_Gwalior_2014-07-13_18-32.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
